WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:06.250
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie, this is going
to be my Doctor Who Episode 10 video.

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:09.560
Even though next week is the beginning of
a two part finale.

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:14.780
The forest story felt like it wasn’t directly
connected to that.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:18.380
We did see Missy again so I’ll try to explain
what I think she was doing.

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:21.630
And just in case I don’t have time to do
a separate video for it I’ll address the

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:23.089
footage in the finale trailer.

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:26.740
Heads up, because I missed last week’s Q&amp;A
video I’m doing a double giveaway for this

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:27.740
week.

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:31.960
All you have to do to participate is be a
subscriber and leave a comment.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:35.250
I’ll explain after we get through all the
WTF.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:39.450
Careful for spoilers if you’re not caught
up, here we go Top 5 Moments

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:42.770
Number 5 - Little Red Riding Hood Finds the
Big Bad Wolf

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:45.710
I guess I shouldn’t be surprised about the
use of Fairy Tales in Doctor Who.

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:50.010
I remember when they made the transition from
Matt Smith to Capaldi a lot of the bigger

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:52.790
blogs were saying this was an end to the Fairy
Tale era.

00:00:52.790 --> 00:01:01.870
But Moffat is really the one who writes the
Fairy Tales, so as long as he’s still running

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:05.840
the show, there will always be elements of
that.

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:12.130
I don’t mind it too much, We got Red Riding
Hood, Hansel and Gretel, the Jungle Book isn’t

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:15.149
so much of a fairy tale but when we saw the
Tiger I thought of Shere Khan.

00:01:15.149 --> 00:01:25.840
Ruyard Kipling 
was a British Author.

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:31.619
In all the preview clips they called it a
magical story.

00:01:31.619 --> 00:01:37.619
I did find it kind of hard to explain the
sister appearing at the end and Maebh’s

00:01:37.619 --> 00:01:40.179
ability to influence reality.

00:01:40.179 --> 00:01:44.200
I kind of had to suspend the rational part
of my brain that searches for explanations.

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:52.740
It’s possible the creatures could be involved
in the finale, the big cutaway at the end

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:57.329
didn’t feel like closure.

00:01:57.329 --> 00:01:59.810
Number 4 - The Earth Protects Itself

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:03.939
The creatures magiced up the trees as a way
to defend against the solar flare.

00:02:03.939 --> 00:02:07.289
The Doctor made it sound like they were protecting
humans but really I think they were just protecting

00:02:07.289 --> 00:02:08.289
the earth itself.

00:02:08.289 --> 00:02:11.819
This was a very Earth Day type story, stop
cutting down the trees.

00:02:11.819 --> 00:02:12.890
They’re trying to help you.

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:18.319
It would have been totally appropriate to
air this during Earth Week but that’s during

00:02:18.319 --> 00:02:20.040
a different part of the year.

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:23.510
Missy was surprised by they outcome, so I
think she might have just been a passive observer

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:24.510
in this episode.

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:26.110
I’ll talk more about her in a sec.

00:02:26.110 --> 00:02:30.020
There’s been so many moments in series 8
where the Doctor has been confronted with

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:31.510
the subject of his longevity.

00:02:31.510 --> 00:02:35.790
Like almost dying permanently last week, the
joke on the moon about not being sure if he

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:39.430
wouldn’t go on regenerating forever when
the astronaut almost shot him.

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:47.200
This week the creatures explained that he
was just blip in their timeline.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:51.930
One of the best lines of the episode was “We
are the life that prevails” - that was actually

00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:53.269
in one of the first series 8 trailers.

00:02:53.269 --> 00:02:56.970
But I think it was the good Dalek that spoke
the line that time.

00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:59.780
This theme about life prevailing is going
to come back in the finale.

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:01.719
So just make a mental note about that.

00:03:01.719 --> 00:03:06.329
Number 3 - Clara and Danny Pink

00:03:06.329 --> 00:03:10.909
Danny apparently still has no idea Clara has
kept up with the Doctor as if nothing has

00:03:10.909 --> 00:03:11.909
changed.

00:03:11.909 --> 00:03:15.760
Given everything we saw in the finale trailer
and how positive he came off in this episode

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:19.750
it totally seems like he’s going to be one
of the tragic heroes of series 8.

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:31.800
Like a Rory type figure and even though there
was the big Clara WTF moment in the trailer,

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:35.780
she did seem like there was a part of her
that bought his line about seeing the things

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:38.040
right in front of you and all the wonders
down here.

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:39.040
Another one of my favorite lines was when
the little girl explained they were yelling

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:40.040
at each other because they loved each other.

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:41.040
There are so many Doctor Who jokes about people
being Scottish and complaining, being angry

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:42.040
but caring deeply.

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:43.040
It all just reminds me of Karen Gillan and
Catherine Tate.

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:44.040
I don’t know if there’s any truth to the
rumors Jenna Coleman is leaving the series,

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:46.069
but you could see all these teasers about
Danny Pink trying to win her over as foreshadowing

00:03:46.069 --> 00:03:49.780
for Clara not traveling with the Doctor any
more and just living a normal life.

00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:51.060
Even in the face of the reveal in the trailer.

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:53.950
Clara never having existed, it’s possible
Moffat could give them a version of a happy

00:03:53.950 --> 00:03:54.950
ending.

00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:56.900
Like Amy and Rory got a twisted kind of happy
ending.

00:03:56.900 --> 00:03:59.099
They were together at least to the end of
their lives.

00:03:59.099 --> 00:04:23.710
Even if they were trapped by the weeping angels.

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:26.560
Number 2 - Class Assignment, Save the Planet

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:29.840
All I could think about when all the children
climbed on board the TARDIS was this was a

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:34.370
Children In Need Special, like they were doing
something that under no circumstances would

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:36.030
happen in normal Doctor Who stories.

00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:40.963
And the wiser children explaining things reminded
me of wesley crusher being the little kid

00:04:40.963 --> 00:04:47.080
on the enterprise surrounded by mostly very
serious adults.

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:50.330
I could see where a lot of people would be
put off by the use of children in the episode,

00:04:50.330 --> 00:04:54.620
but given the fairy tale aspect of the story,
Maebh and the Coal Hill field trip I think

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:55.620
it worked.

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:59.620
The Doctor didn’t seek the children out,
Maebh sought him out.

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:01.050
She even knocked on the TARDIS door.

00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:04.710
It’s one of those rare moments when you
know someone is special.

00:05:04.710 --> 00:05:07.870
Like when The Doctor explained GUS from Orient
Express had phoned the TARDIS.

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:10.870
There are just some things that no one is
supposed to be able to do.

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:15.389
So when someone new is able to track down
The Doctor it’s really interesting.

00:05:15.389 --> 00:05:16.500
Missy even had that line.

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:19.150
“This is a surprise, I like Suprises”

00:05:19.150 --> 00:05:23.060
and my Number 1 WTF Moment - The Finale Trailer

00:05:23.060 --> 00:05:26.550
Since I might not have time to get an extra
video out just for the trailer we have to

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:28.280
talk about it.

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:29.550
First off, the Cybermen.

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:31.270
Worst kept secret this year.

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:35.400
The BBC even posted pictures of them to their
official page, they brought Cybermen with

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:37.100
them on the World Tour.

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:41.260
I saw they cybermen spoilers when they were
filming many many months ago.

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:47.270
I know a lot of you saw them too.

00:05:47.270 --> 00:06:03.650
It was really hard to omit them and the details
about Missy from my series 8 videos.

00:06:03.650 --> 00:06:05.940
Now we can finally talk about almost everything.

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:10.100
There are still a few spoilers that weren’t
in that trailer.

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:16.120
So please use spoiler tags for cyber conversion
related things.

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:18.820
All those cybermen have to come from somewhere.

00:06:18.820 --> 00:06:23.030
Second, Clara Owald never existed.

00:06:23.030 --> 00:06:29.639
Very shocking claim, so it’s possible that
Clara is like a tesselecta or advanced cyberman

00:06:29.639 --> 00:06:30.639
that Missy is operating.

00:06:30.639 --> 00:06:36.130
Or she’s like Mr Clever, an advanced version
of the Cyber Controller that doesn’t look

00:06:36.130 --> 00:06:37.510
like a cyberman.

00:06:37.510 --> 00:06:44.139
They’ve had human form Daleks, of course
they can do the same thing with Cybermen if

00:06:44.139 --> 00:06:45.139
they wanted.

00:06:45.139 --> 00:06:48.889
Either way, Missy is controlling Clara.

00:06:48.889 --> 00:06:52.560
If missy really was sitting inside a Cybermen,
with the little eye behind her here there’s

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:54.389
still a lot to explain.

00:06:54.389 --> 00:06:58.270
But she’s walking around with The Doctor
here.

00:06:58.270 --> 00:07:01.280
So there’s still a big question about the
nethersphere.

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:05.520
They kept talking about Invasion and things
living in-between universes.

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:06.520
Like the creatures in this episode.

00:07:06.520 --> 00:07:08.509
They exist in between the spaces in reality.

00:07:08.509 --> 00:07:10.360
So The Doctor saying “The Invasion is over”
it’s already won seems kind of prophetic.

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:16.159
It makes it seem like missy is going to spring
cybermen everywhere instantaneously and it’s

00:07:16.159 --> 00:07:18.830
going to involve some alternate dimension
jumping.

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:22.330
Like the nethersphere is a pocket universe
type alternate reality like the forest creatures

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:23.330
live in.

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:55.180
Lots of theories to make but Clara Betrayal,
Missy Invasion and what does it all have to

00:07:55.180 --> 00:08:07.030
do with The Doctor being Missy’s boyfriend.

00:08:07.030 --> 00:08:16.000
Let me know what your favorite moment was
and for the Q&amp;A, I will do 

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:22.050
a Q&amp;A for this.

00:08:22.050 --> 00:08:31.009
Just remember, Clara is seen emerging from
one of these Cyberman chambers, in this scene

00:08:31.009 --> 00:08:52.790
she’s got a cyberman pointing a gun at her
and UNIT is a big part 

00:08:52.790 --> 00:09:13.040
of 

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:14.040
the story.

00:09:14.040 --> 00:09:33.990
So I think it will be 
a 

00:09:33.990 --> 00:09:54.930
lot 
more complicated that Clara just being 

00:09:54.930 --> 00:10:06.430
a 

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:34.740
Missy Puppet.

